# The cspell dictionary is one alphabetically sorted word per line, so two
# branches that each add a word collide at the same line by construction — a
# conflict whose only correct resolution is "keep both sides". `merge=union`
# is git's built-in driver for exactly that, so never hand-resolve a conflict
# in this file.
#
# Union merge neither sorts nor de-duplicates, and it keeps a line the other
# side DELETED. The first two heal at the next `make lint`; the third does
# not heal at all and is accepted. Sound here ONLY because the dictionary is
# an unordered set that happens to be stored sorted — do not extend the
# attribute to a file where a dropped, doubled, or reordered line changes
# meaning.
#
# The full argument lives in docs/conventions/docs-and-style.md under
# "Spelling (cspell)". Keep it there, not here: two prose copies of one
# rationale is the drift generator this very file exists to remove.
cfg/dictionary.txt merge=union
